// error
// `stackMapsBegin()`/`stackMapsEnd()` (§11.12) are zero-arity by construction: a
// link produces exactly ONE stack-map table (ABI.md §4), so there is nothing to
// select and no argument that could mean anything.
//
// The refusal lives in the checker rather than in lowering, on the same footing
// as `entryOf`'s: the alternative is a program that passes `bit check` and then
// emits a relocation whose operand was silently discarded.
fn main() {
  print("${int(stackMapsBegin(1))}")
  print("${int(stackMapsEnd(1, 2))}")
}
